cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Robo Use in your research, please cite it as below, and cite the benchmarks your tasks come from."
title: "Robo Use: agent as a policy for embodied agents"
abstract: "Robo Use turns robot benchmarks into tasks that a coding agent, such as Claude Code or Codex, solves by driving a simulated robot from its shell with the robo command. An episode server owns the simulator, enforces the step budget, records a video and scores the final physical state. The package contains 790 tasks in 34 suites, adapted from Meta-World, LIBERO, robosuite, RoboCasa, Gymnasium-Robotics, dm_control, MyoSuite, HumanoidBench, MuJoCo Menagerie and other sources, as BenchFlow task folders."
type: software
